/!--
The other way to add JavaScript to your page is by linking a JavaScript file. For this, we also use the script tag. Except, we put a src attribute in the opening tag. Like this:
<script src="index.js"></script>

Add a script tag to link the index.js file in the <head> tag.

Note: we don't support multiple files on the platform so we can't write any code in index.js. You can try this locally on your computer though.
--/

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width">
    <title>repl.it</title>
    <!-- Add your script tag below -->
    <script src="index.js"></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>JavaScript doesn't bite.</h1>
  </body>
</html>